; dpa cdylib export whitelist.
;
; The dpa core library exposes no C ABI contract of its own: the plugin ABI
; (dpa_plugin_*) lives inside plugin crates via the dpa_plugin! export macro,
; and the host consumes plugins through libloading + an explicit symbol list.
; Rust cdylibs only re-export #[no_mangle] / #[export_name] items, but C
; libraries statically linked into the DLL (e.g. bzip2's bz_internal_error)
; can still leak into the export table.
;
; An explicit /DEF: with an EMPTY EXPORTS section hides every symbol, keeping
; the DLL export surface at zero. Any future dpa_ffi contract MUST be listed
; here explicitly (and covered by tests/plugin_smoke.rs).
EXPORTS
